# HTSA pre-call resource pages — NEW pages only

## Trigger

CJ says **"pre call link"** (or "precall page", "resource page") and pastes some or all of:
name, email, phone, day, date, time.

Then do everything below without asking follow-up questions. If something is
missing, use the fallbacks in the Missing info table and say what you assumed.

**They already have a call booked.** That is what this page is for. Never render
"Let's find 45 minutes" or any booking copy unless CJ explicitly says they still
need to schedule.

## Read `.cursor/rules/htsa-page-map.mdc` first

That file disambiguates CJ's four page types. If he said anything other than
"pre call link", you may be in the wrong rule.

## What this page is for

The person has **already booked**. A setter or a marketing lead scheduled them and
they already have the calendar invite. This page is not for booking. Its job is
show-up rate and arriving pre-framed. CJ texts the link the day before.

## Never hand-rebuild

Always copy the template. Never write a pre-call page from scratch, and never
"improve" the template's layout, CSS, copy, or tracking while making someone's page.

```
SOURCE:  r/_TEMPLATE-precall.html
OUTPUT:  r/<first>_<last>/index.html
```

Folder name is lowercase, underscore separated: `r/test_person/index.html`
Live URL becomes `https://closewithcjclay.com/r/test_person/`

## Step 1 — copy, then edit ONLY these two places

**A. The GUEST block** near the bottom of the `<script>`:

```js
const GUEST = {
  firstName:  "Test",
  fullName:   "Test Person",
  email:      "test@example.com",
  phone:      "+15555550100",                     // E.164, keep the +1
  slug:       "test_person",                      // MUST match the folder name
  booked:     true,                               // ALWAYS true unless CJ explicitly says they still need to book
  callLabel:  "Wednesday, Sept 2 · 10:00 AM EST", // exactly how it reads on the page
  confirmDay: "Wednesday",                        // one word, used on the confirm button
  bookingUrl: "https://meetings.hubspot.com/charles660/cj"
};
```

`slug` drives the tracking rows in CJ's sheet. If it does not match the folder
name, his analytics break silently. Check it.

**B. One line in `<head>`:**

```html
<meta property="og:url" content="https://closewithcjclay.com/r/test_person/">
```

Change nothing else. Not the layout, not the CSS, not the copy, not the
`recordResourcePageEvent` tracking code.

## Missing info fallbacks

| Missing | Do this |
|---|---|
| Last name | Use first name only for the slug: `r/test/` |
| Email or phone | Leave the empty string. Tracking still works, those columns are just blank. |
| Time zone | Assume EST and write EST in `callLabel` |
| Day/date/time entirely | **Still `booked: true`.** Leave `callLabel` and `confirmDay` empty. The date block hides itself. CJ pasting only name, email and number means he did not paste the time, NOT that they need to book. |

## Step 2 — assets (already exist, do not touch)

These are root absolute on purpose. The page sits one folder deep, so relative
paths break it. Never re-path, rename, inline, or "optimize" them:

```
/cj-headshot-600.png                     header photo + footer business card
/media/this-week-at-htsa-2026-08-18.mp4  the Aug 18 placement clip
/media/htsa-clip-poster.jpg              its poster frame
/r/og-precall.jpg                        link preview card
```

## Step 3 — video rules, do not break these

1. The Aug 18 clip keeps `preload="metadata"` **and** the `poster` attribute.
   `preload="none"` with no working poster gives the browser no dimensions, and the
   element collapses to a black 300x150 box. This has already broken once.
2. Keep `aspect-ratio: 16/9` on `.video-frame video` at every width. Never add an
   `aspect-ratio: auto` override in the mobile media query.
3. The two YouTube videos must play **inside the page**. They are click to load
   `<button class="yt">` facades that swap in a youtube-nocookie iframe on tap.
   Never convert them to `<a href>` links. Never add `target="_blank"`.
   Keep the params exactly: `?autoplay=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&playsinline=1`
   `playsinline` is what stops iOS from hijacking to fullscreen or the YouTube app.
4. Only the `.link-row` items (Trustpilot, Top 20 PDF, HTSA site) and the footer
   links may open a new tab.

## Step 4 — verify before reporting done

1. Header photo and footer card photo both render.
2. Aug 18 clip shows its poster immediately, 16:9, not black.
3. Both YouTube thumbnails load. Tapping one plays in page without navigating away.
4. `slug` matches the folder name, and `og:url` matches the real path.
5. No console errors. No horizontal scroll at 375px.
6. Confirm button reads "Confirm I'll be there" and becomes
   "Confirmed, see you <confirmDay>" on click.

## Step 5 — ship it

New files are untracked. Always finish with:

```bash
cd ~/Desktop/closewithcjclay.com/closewithcjclay.com
git add r/<first>_<last>/
git commit -m "Add pre-call page for <Full Name>"
git push
```

Then give CJ the live URL and tell him to load it once himself before texting it.
GitHub Pages takes about a minute.

## Step 6 — output the ready to send messages

**TWO texts. Never three.** The URL lives in Message 1, not in its own
message. Do not add a third text. Do not add "See you <day> at <time>"
onto Text 2. Do not ask if he wants these. Print them every time.

**Follow `no-dashes-in-client-copy.mdc`. No em dashes, no en dashes, no hyphen
dashes as punctuation anywhere in these. Commas and periods only.**

Substitute the real name, slug, day and time. Use CJ's voice: plain, warm, no hype.

**Never write a negative descriptive norm about other prospects.** Do not write
"most people don't", "hardly anyone replies", "you'd be surprised how few show up",
or anything similar.

Print TEXT and EMAIL as a black-on-white HTML block he can paste into
iMessage, Gmail, and HubSpot. Clickable links. No markdown. No code fences.

